\import{fdip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Remark}
\title{How to read these notes}
\date{2026-10-31}

\p{The displayed order is a safe reading route. Its first box groups
the eight foundation chapters, from [fields on finite carriers](fdip-0015) to
[constrained Gaussian laws](fdip-003V); it does not make every foundation
a premise of every later result. Solid arrows show selected uses of
definitions and results, not all prerequisites. The dashed route is
optional context for relative precision. Each statement names its
precise assumptions.}

\texfig{\begin{tikzpicture}[
  box/.style={draw,rounded corners=2pt,align=center,font=\small,
    text width=27mm,minimum height=10mm,inner sep=3pt},
  flow/.style={-{Stealth[length=2mm]},semithick}
]
\node[box,text width=41mm] (foundation) at (0,0)
  {Foundations\\first eight chapters};
\node[box] (retained) at (0,-1.4) {Retained laws};
\node[box] (background) at (0,-2.8) {Backgrounds};
\node[box] (sector) at (-2,-4.3) {Sectors};
\node[box] (clifford) at (1.7,-4.3) {Clifford algebras};
\node[box] (dirac) at (1.7,-6) {Spatial Dirac};
\node[box] (enriched) at (1.7,-7.8) {Enriched comparison};
\node[box] (arithmetic) at (1.7,-9.6) {Arithmetic};
\node[box] (synthesis) at (-2,-9.6) {Synthesis};
\draw[flow] (foundation) -- (retained);
\draw[flow] (retained) -- (background);
\draw[flow] (background.south) -- (0,-3.5) -| (sector.north);
\draw[flow] (background.south) -- (0,-3.5) -| (clifford.north);
\draw[flow] (clifford) -- (dirac);
\draw[flow] (clifford.east) -- (3.5,-4.3) |- (enriched.east);
\draw[flow] (clifford.east) -- (3.9,-4.3) |- (arithmetic.east);
\draw[flow] (sector) -- (synthesis);
\draw[flow] (dirac.west) -- (-0.15,-6) -- (synthesis.north east);
\draw[flow] (enriched.west) -- (-0.15,-7.8) -- (synthesis.east);
\draw[flow] (arithmetic.west) -- (synthesis.east);
\draw[flow,dashed] (enriched.south) -- node[right,font=\scriptsize]
  {context} (arithmetic.north);
\end{tikzpicture}}

\p{[Retained laws](fdip-0018) combine Schur elimination and Gaussian
integration; [backgrounds](fdip-0019) then specify which data and laws
are transported. [Sectors](fdip-001A) and [Clifford algebras](fdip-001B)
use these constructions; the sector comparison is restated locally in
the Clifford chapter. [Spatial Dirac](fdip-001C),
[enriched comparison](fdip-001E) and [arithmetic](fdip-001D) develop
different subsequent questions, with relative precision restated in the
arithmetic setting. The [synthesis](fdip-003W) compares their results
with the conjecture. The opening motivation and forward example links
orient these readings without adding hypotheses.}
